 "admissions_overview": {
  "summary": "To start an official university degree (grado) in Spain you must pass an access test, the PAU (also called EBAU or selectividad in some regions), normally taken after bachillerato. The mandatory phase has four exams (five in regions with a co-official language): Spanish Language and Literature II, History of Spain or History of Philosophy, a foreign language, and a subject from your bachillerato track. After that you apply for places through your region's pre-enrolment system, for example the single district of Madrid for the public universities there.",
  "official_url": "https://web.ua.es/en/oia/faq/pruebas-de-acceso-a-la-universidad-pau.html",
  "notes": "PAU dates, exam format and how marks are used for admission are set each year and differ by autonomous community. Check your regional university access office and each university's pre-enrolment page. Degree names are given in English with the Spanish or Catalan name in the note."
 },
